  "notes": "Thomson T32RTL6000 (manufacturer SCBC, Realtek platform), Android TV 9 (API 28), 1.5 GB\nRAM, 1280x720 output. Firmware PTT1.210114.001 build 337 (2021-04-25), security patch 2021-03-05.\nThe OS itself reports model/device strings \"ATV R1\"/\"R1\" on this TV — same hardware:\nfingerprint THOMSON/THOMSON/R1:9/PTT1.210114.001/337:user/release-keys\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/thomson-t32rtl6000/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/thomson-t32rtl6000/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nSame platform family as examples/sanyo-atv-r2/ (SCBC, PTT1.x firmware branch): the SANYO\nlist cross-checks several decisions here (the GDPR consent agent, and FastScreen being a\nFastCast Miracast receiver rather than a launcher on this family).\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (restore.sh / build-and-install.sh defaults work).\nLive TV app: com.android.tv with the Realtek tuner stack (com.realtek.dtv and friends) —\nthe tuner must stay enabled or live channels disappear.\nTvProvider quirk: on this firmware the system TvProvider stays empty — the vendor tuner\nkeeps channels and EPG in its own store, so launcher channel rows are dormant until the\nprovider fills (e.g. after a firmware update).\nKept on purpose: GMS / Play / WebView / keyboard, the tuner stack above, remote/Bluetooth\n(com.apps.smartkey, bluetoothremote, fivekey, virtualkey, autopair),\ncom.creative.fastscreen.tv (FastCast Miracast receiver on this family — NOT a FastScreen\nad app, do not disable it as one), and streaming apps left to taste.\n--- Telemetry, analytics, recommendation rows ---",
